  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>A plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;contains the line of intersection of the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math>,</p><p>Now let,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>So, by family of planes concept we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Also given plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Hence, equation of plane will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now distance of point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from plane will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mn>12</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mfenced><mn>12</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mn>18</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>81</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>And square of distance will be,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mn>12</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mfenced><mn>12</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mn>18</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>81</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>310</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>310</mn></mrow><mn>155</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>620</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
